**Summary of behavior:** The new `xcrunCommand()` method (per its doc comment) returns just `"xcrun"` on x86 macOS and prepends `"/usr/bin/arch", "-arm64"` on ARM macOS to run Xcode commands outside Rosetta. The ARM detection relies on `_operatingSystemUtils.hostPlatform == HostPlatform.darwin_arm` (which the tests exercise via a `sysctl hw.optional.arm64` command). The hardcoded `/usr/bin/xcrun` / `xcrun` strings in `eulaSigned`, `isSimctlInstalled`, `cc`, `clang`, and `sdkLocation` were replaced with `...xcrunCommand()`. In `XCDevice`, the `xcdevicePath` getter and its `xcrun --find xcdevice` lookup were removed, and `isInstalled` was simplified to just check `_xcode.isInstalledAndMeetsVersionCheck`.

